{"title": "Sectional Mock #77 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>If the universal set U = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14}, set A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}, and set B = {3, 6, 9, 12, 15}, then find the number of elements in set U  -  {A  -  B}.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2351; U = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14}, &#2360;&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2351; A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2351; B = {3, 6, 9, 12, 15} &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2351; U - {A - B} &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4", "3", "5", "2"], "options_hi": ["4", "3", "5", "2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>U = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14}</p><p>A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}</p><p>B = {3, 6, 9, 12, 15}</p><p>So, A  -  B = {1, 2, 4, 5}</p><p>And U  -  (A  -  B) = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14} - {1, 2, 4, 5}</p><p>= (6, 8, 10, 12, 14)</p><p>So, n(U  -  (A  -  B)) = 5.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>U = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14}</p><p>A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}</p><p>B = {3, 6, 9, 12, 15}</p><p>So, A  -  B = {1, 2, 4, 5}</p><p>And U  -  (A  -  B) = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14} - {1, 2, 4, 5}</p><p>= (6, 8, 10, 12, 14)</p><p>So, n(U  -  (A  -  B)) = 5.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a parallelogram the length of the adjacent sides are 12 cm and 14 cm respectively. If the length of one diagonal is 16 cm then what is the approximate length of the other diagonal?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["14.56 cm", "17.5 cm", "20.6 cm", "22 cm"], "options_hi": ["14.56 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "17.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "20.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "22 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We know that in a parallelogram</p><p>Sum of the squares of the diagonals = 2(sum of the squares of the two adjacent sides)</p><p>Let the length of the other diagonal be = D cm</p><p>Therefore; D<sup>2</sup> + 16<sup>2</sup> = 2(12<sup>2</sup>+ 14<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; D<sup>2</sup> + 256 = 2(144+ 196)</p><p>=&gt; D<sup>2</sup> = 680  -  256 = 424</p><p>=&gt; D = 20.6 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that in a parallelogram</p><p>Sum of the squares of the diagonals = 2(sum of the squares of the two adjacent sides)</p><p>Let the length of the other diagonal be = D cm</p><p>Therefore; D<sup>2</sup> + 16<sup>2</sup> = 2(12<sup>2</sup>+ 14<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; D<sup>2</sup> + 256 = 2(144+ 196)</p><p>=&gt; D<sup>2</sup> = 680  -  256 = 424</p><p>=&gt; D = 20.6 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two trains are moving in the same direction at 60 km/h and 42 km/h. The faster train crosses a man in the slower train in 36 seconds. Find the length of the faster train. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 42 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2343;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; 36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["185 m", "180 m", "195 m", "175 m"], "options_hi": ["185 &#2350;&#2368;", "180 &#2350;&#2368;", "195 &#2350;&#2368;", "175 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Relative speed = 60 - 42 = 18 km/h = 5 m/s </p><p>Length of the faster train = 5 * 36 = 180 m </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative speed = 60 - 42 = 18 km/h = 5 m/s </p><p>Length of the faster train = 5 * 36 = 180 m </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average of all numbers from 113 to 959 which is multiple of 7 and 9 is ________.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>113 &#2360;&#2375; 959 &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2332;&#2379; 7 &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; __________ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["524.5", "545.5", "535.5", "534.5"], "options_hi": ["524.5", "545.5", "535.5", "534.5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>All the numbers between 113 to 959 which is multiple of 7 and 9 i.e., 63 = (126, 189, 252, .., 945)</p><p>Number of terms = (945  -  126)/63 + 1 = 14</p><p>Sum = 14/2 * (126 + 945) = 7497</p><p>So, required average = 7497/14 = 535.5</p><p>Alternate method:</p><p>Average of an A.P = (last number + first number)/2</p><p>Required average = (126 + 945)/2 = 535.5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>All the numbers between 113 to 959 which is multiple of 7 and 9 i.e., 63 = (126, 189, 252, .., 945)</p><p>Number of terms = (945  -  126)/63 + 1 = 14</p><p>Sum = 14/2 * (126 + 945) = 7497</p><p>So, required average = 7497/14 = 535.5</p><p>Alternate method:</p><p>Average of an A.P = (last number + first number)/2</p><p>Required average = (126 + 945)/2 = 535.5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = ab + bc + ca, then find the value of</p><p>(25a<sup>4</sup> + 15b<sup>4</sup> + 18c<sup>4</sup>)/(128a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 56b<sup>2</sup>c<sup>2</sup> + 48c<sup>2</sup>a<sup>2</sup>) is :</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = ab + bc + ca, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;</p><p>(25a<sup>4</sup> + 15b<sup>4</sup> + 18c<sup>4</sup>)/(128a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 56b<sup>2</sup>c<sup>2</sup> + 48c<sup>2</sup>a<sup>2</sup>) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["4", "1", "0.5", "0.25"], "options_hi": ["4", "1", "0.5", "0.25"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = ab + bc + ca</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> + (b  -  c)<sup>2</sup> + (c  -  a)<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>a = b = c</p><p>let a = b = c = k then,</p><p>25a<sup>4</sup> + 15b<sup>4</sup> + 18c<sup>4</sup> = 25k<sup>4</sup> + 15k<sup>4</sup> + 18k<sup>4</sup> = 58k<sup>4</sup></p><p>128a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 56b<sup>2</sup>c<sup>2</sup> + 48c<sup>2</sup>a<sup>2</sup> = 128k<sup>4</sup> + 56k<sup>4</sup> + 48k<sup>4</sup> = 232k<sup>4</sup></p><p>(25a<sup>4</sup> + 15b<sup>4</sup> + 18c<sup>4</sup>)/(128a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 56b<sup>2</sup>c<sup>2</sup> + 48c<sup>2</sup>a<sup>2</sup>) = 58/232</p><p>=&gt; 58/232 = 1/4 or 0.25</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = ab + bc + ca</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> + (b  -  c)<sup>2</sup> + (c  -  a)<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>a = b = c</p><p>let a = b = c = k then,</p><p>25a<sup>4</sup> + 15b<sup>4</sup> + 18c<sup>4</sup> = 25k<sup>4</sup> + 15k<sup>4</sup> + 18k<sup>4</sup> = 58k<sup>4</sup></p><p>128a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 56b<sup>2</sup>c<sup>2</sup> + 48c<sup>2</sup>a<sup>2</sup> = 128k<sup>4</sup> + 56k<sup>4</sup> + 48k<sup>4</sup> = 232k<sup>4</sup></p><p>(25a<sup>4</sup> + 15b<sup>4</sup> + 18c<sup>4</sup>)/(128a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 56b<sup>2</sup>c<sup>2</sup> + 48c<sup>2</sup>a<sup>2</sup>) = 58/232</p><p>=&gt; 58/232 = 1/4 or 0.25</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A thief takes off on his bike at a certain speed, after seeing a police car at a distance of 250 m. The police car starts chasing the thief and catches him. If the thief runs 1.5 km before being caught and the speed of the police car is 70 km/h, then what is the speed of thief's bike (in km/h)?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352; 250 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352; &#2346;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 1.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 70 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["65 km/h", "60 km/h", "55 km/h", "50 km/h"], "options_hi": ["65 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "55 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "50 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Convert 250 m to km: 250 m = 0.25 km.</p><p>The thief covers an extra 1.5 km after the police start chasing.</p><p>Let the thief's speed be v km/h. Then, his time = 1.5/v hours.</p><p>In the same time, the police cover the thief's extra 1.5 km plus the initial 0.25 km head start, total 1.75 km.</p><p>Since the police speed is 70 km/h, their time = 1.75/70 hours.</p><p>Equate the times: 1.5/v = 1.75/70.</p><p>Solve for v:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;v = (1.5  X  70) / 1.75 = 105 / 1.75 = 60 km/h.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Convert 250 m to km: 250 m = 0.25 km.</p><p>The thief covers an extra 1.5 km after the police start chasing.</p><p>Let the thief's speed be v km/h. Then, his time = 1.5/v hours.</p><p>In the same time, the police cover the thief's extra 1.5 km plus the initial 0.25 km head start, total 1.75 km.</p><p>Since the police speed is 70 km/h, their time = 1.75/70 hours.</p><p>Equate the times: 1.5/v = 1.75/70.</p><p>Solve for v:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;v = (1.5  X  70) / 1.75 = 105 / 1.75 = 60 km/h.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>Solve the following expression <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;: <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>1", "options_en": ["1", "2cos<sup>2</sup>&#952;", "0", "2sec<sup>2</sup>&#952;"], "options_hi": ["1", "2cos<sup>2</sup>&#952;", "0", "2sec<sup>2</sup>&#952;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>1/(1 + sin&#952;) + 1/(1 -&nbsp;sin&#952;)&nbsp;</p><p><span>= [(1 - sin&#952; + 1 + sin&#952;) / (1 - sin</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#952;)]</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;= 2/cos</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;&#952;</span></p><p><span>= 2sec</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;&#952;</span></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>1/(1 + sin&#952;) + 1/(1 -&nbsp;sin&#952;)&nbsp;</p><p><span>= [(1 - sin&#952; + 1 + sin&#952;) / (1 - sin</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#952;)]</span></p><p><span>&nbsp;= 2/cos</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;&#952;</span></p><p><span>= 2sec</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&#160;&#952;</span></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Marks scored by a student in different subjects are given in the table below</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Subjects</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Marks obtained out of 100</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">English</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">55</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Hindi</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">90</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Mathematics</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">75</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Science</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">80</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Foreign language</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">90</td></tr></table><p>Five marks are to be deducted from each subject due to shortage of attendance. The net average of the mean, median and mode of the marks obtained is<u>_____.</u></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">100 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364;&#2368;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">55</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">90</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2327;&#2339;&#2367;&#2340;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">75</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">80</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2366;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">90</td></tr></table><p>&#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;, &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340;_____ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["79.33", "77.67", "82.66", "73"], "options_hi": ["79.33", "77.67", "82.66", "73"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>New marks in English, Hindi, Mathematics, Science, and foreign language after deduction are 50, 85, 70, 75, and 85 respectively.</p><p>Marks in ascending order = 50, 70, 75, 85, 85</p><p>Mean = (50 + 85 + 70 + 75 + 85)/5 = 365/5 = 73</p><p>Median = (5 + 1)/2<sup>th</sup> term = 3<sup>rd</sup> term = 75</p><p>Mode = 85</p><p>Required average = (73 + 75 + 85)/3</p><p>= 233/3</p><p>= 77.67</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>New marks in English, Hindi, Mathematics, Science, and foreign language after deduction are 50, 85, 70, 75, and 85 respectively.</p><p>Marks in ascending order = 50, 70, 75, 85, 85</p><p>Mean = (50 + 85 + 70 + 75 + 85)/5 = 365/5 = 73</p><p>Median = (5 + 1)/2<sup>th</sup> term = 3<sup>rd</sup> term = 75</p><p>Mode = 85</p><p>Required average = (73 + 75 + 85)/3</p><p>= 233/3</p><p>= 77.67</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum amounts to Rs.14000 after 7 years and to Rs.20000 after 14 years at a certain compound interest compounded annually. Find the sum.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 7 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 14000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 14 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 20000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; (&#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2343;&#2344;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.9800", "Rs.8400", "Rs.11200", "Rs.9600"], "options_hi": ["9800 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "8400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "11200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "9600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p><img width=175 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=147 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=175 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=136 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=129 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=85 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image013.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p><img width=175 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=147 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=175 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=136 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=129 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=85 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23231/image013.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Area of a rhombus is 96 cm<sup>2</sup> and length of its one diagonal is 12 cm. Find the length of side of rhombus.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 96 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 12 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["15 cm", "20 cm", "10 cm", "12 cm"], "options_hi": ["15 cm", "20 cm", "10 cm", "12 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Area of rhombus = (1/2) * Product of its diagonal</p><p>96= (1/2) * d<sub>1</sub> * d<sub>2</sub></p><p>192 = 12 * d<sub>2</sub></p><p>d<sub>2</sub> = 16 cm</p><p>Length of side of rhombus = &radic;[(16/2)<sup>2</sup> + (12/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 10 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of rhombus = (1/2) * Product of its diagonal</p><p>96= (1/2) * d<sub>1</sub> * d<sub>2</sub></p><p>192 = 12 * d<sub>2</sub></p><p>d<sub>2</sub> = 16 cm</p><p>Length of side of rhombus = &radic;[(16/2)<sup>2</sup> + (12/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 10 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cube of side length X cm is melted and recast into a cuboid of dimensions 15 cm x 24 cm x 75 cm. Find the lateral surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of cube.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; 15 cm x 24 cm x 75 cm &#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2338;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2400", "4800", "3600", "3000"], "options_hi": ["2400", "4800", "3600", "3000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cube = Volume of cuboid</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 15 x 24 x 75</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 5 x 3 x 3 x 8 x 5 x 5 x 3</p><p>X = 30 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of cube = 4 * X<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4 x 30 x 30</p><p>= 3600 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cube = Volume of cuboid</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 15 x 24 x 75</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 5 x 3 x 3 x 8 x 5 x 5 x 3</p><p>X = 30 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of cube = 4 * X<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4 x 30 x 30</p><p>= 3600 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (a + 5) is an odd number, then what are the two other even numbers nearest to it?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>45 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; 8 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2344;&#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["a + 4, a + 3", "a, a - 1", "a + 1, a + 2", "a + 2, a + 4"], "options_hi": ["64&#8731;15", "32&#8731;15", "64&#8731;5", "16&#8731;15"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>9 men and 3 women sit at a round table. In how many ways can they sit if 3 women must sit together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>9 &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2376;&#2336; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["2!*8!", "3!*8!", "3!*9!", "2!*9!"], "options_hi": ["2!*8!", "3!*8!", "3!*9!", "2!*9!"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Number of men = 9</p><p>Number of women = 3</p><p>Total number of ways = 3! * 9!</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of men = 9</p><p>Number of women = 3</p><p>Total number of ways = 3! * 9!</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>In Big Bazar, a Jeans is marked 30% above the cost price but during Diwali sale, it is sold at 15% discount. Thus, 60 Jeans are sold for total Rs. 53040. Find the actual cost price of the Jeans.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2348;&#2367;&#2327; &#2348;&#2366;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2368;&#2344;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 30% &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2351;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 15% &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;, 60 &#2332;&#2368;&#2344;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 53040 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2332;&#2368;&#2306;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 800", "Rs. 850", "Rs. 750", "Rs. 900"], "options_hi": ["800 &#2352;&#2369;", "850 &#2352;&#2369;", "750 &#2352;&#2369;", "900 &#2352;&#2369;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Since 60 Jeans are sold for total Rs. 53040</p><p>Selling price of a Jeans during sale = 53040/60 = Rs. 884</p><p>Since 15% discount is offered:</p><p>Marked price of the Jeans = 884/0.85 = Rs. 1040</p><p>Cost price of the Jeans = 1040/1.3 = Rs. 800</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since 60 Jeans are sold for total Rs. 53040</p><p>Selling price of a Jeans during sale = 53040/60 = Rs. 884</p><p>Since 15% discount is offered:</p><p>Marked price of the Jeans = 884/0.85 = Rs. 1040</p><p>Cost price of the Jeans = 1040/1.3 = Rs. 800</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sheena has 5 English mock tests, 3 Reasoning mock tests and 8 Quant mock tests from which she chooses a mock test. In how many ways can she select 1 English mock test, 1 Reasoning mock test and 1 Quant mock test?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 5 &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;, 3 &#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;, 1 &#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 1 &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335; &#2350;&#2377;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["140", "100", "60", "120"], "options_hi": ["140", "100", "60", "120"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Number of English mock tests = 5</p><p>Number of Reasoning mock tests = 3</p><p>Number of Quant mock tests = 8</p><p>Total number of ways = 5*3*8 = 120</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of English mock tests = 5</p><p>Number of Reasoning mock tests = 3</p><p>Number of Quant mock tests = 8</p><p>Total number of ways = 5*3*8 = 120</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Following line graph shows the number of cars of various colours manufactured by two brands Tata and Mahindra. What is the sum of number of total Black cars manufactured and the total Red cars manufactured?</p><p><img width=357 height=263 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25004/image009.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2337; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2340; &#2335;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"357\" height=\"263\" id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25004/image009.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["800", "900", "920", "800"], "options_hi": ["800", "900", "920", "850"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total black cars manufactured = 240 + 320 = 560</p><p>Total red cars manufactured = 160 + 180 = 340</p><p>Required sum = 560 + 340 = 900</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total black cars manufactured = 240 + 320 = 560</p><p>Total red cars manufactured = 160 + 180 = 340</p><p>Required sum = 560 + 340 = 900</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of time taken by Gaurav to that by Saurav is 7:9 for the same length of race. If Gaurav beats Saurav by 150 m, then what is the length of race course?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2380;&#2352;&#2357; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2380;&#2352;&#2357; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7:9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2327;&#2380;&#2352;&#2357; &#2360;&#2380;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; 150 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["735 m", "640 m", "675 m", "700 m"], "options_hi": ["735 &#2350;&#2368;", "640 &#2350;&#2368;", "675 &#2350;&#2368;", "700 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Time taken by Gaurav : Time taken by Saurav = 7:9</p><p>Speed of Gaurav : speed of Saurav = 9:7</p><p>Length of race course = 150 * 9/(9  -  7) = 675 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time taken by Gaurav : Time taken by Saurav = 7:9</p><p>Speed of Gaurav : speed of Saurav = 9:7</p><p>Length of race course = 150 * 9/(9  -  7) = 675 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (2p + 1)<sup>3</sup> + (4p  -  9)<sup>3</sup> + (p + 6)<sup>3</sup> = (2p + 1)(4p  -  9)(3p + 18) and p &#8800; 5, then what is the value of p?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (2p + 1)<sup>3</sup> + (4p  -  9)<sup>3</sup> + (p + 6)<sup>3</sup> = (2p + 1)(4p  -  9)(3p + 18) &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; p &ne; 5 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; p &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2/7", "2/9", "1/9", "2/3"], "options_hi": ["2/7", "2/9", "1/9", "2/3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>(2p + 1)<sup>3</sup> + (4p  -  9)<sup>3</sup> + (p + 6)<sup>3</sup> = (2p + 1)(4p  -  9)(3p + 18)</p><p>(2p + 1)<sup>3</sup> + (4p  -  9)<sup>3</sup> + (p + 6)<sup>3</sup> = 3(2p + 1)(4p  -  9)(p + 6)</p><p>When x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 3xyz, then x + y + z = 0</p><p>(2p + 1) + (4p  -  9) + (p + 6) = 0</p><p>7p = 2</p><p>p = 2/7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(2p + 1)<sup>3</sup> + (4p  -  9)<sup>3</sup> + (p + 6)<sup>3</sup> = (2p + 1)(4p  -  9)(3p + 18)</p><p>(2p + 1)<sup>3</sup> + (4p  -  9)<sup>3</sup> + (p + 6)<sup>3</sup> = 3(2p + 1)(4p  -  9)(p + 6)</p><p>When x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 3xyz, then x + y + z = 0</p><p>(2p + 1) + (4p  -  9) + (p + 6) = 0</p><p>7p = 2</p><p>p = 2/7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The unit digit of (147<sup>11</sup>)<sup>13</sup> is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(147<sup>11</sup>)<sup>13</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["3", "7", "1", "9"], "options_hi": ["3", "7", "1", "9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=116 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image007.png\"></p><p>We know, that cyclicity of 7 is 4</p><p>So, when we divide 143 by 4 we get 3 as reminder,</p><p>Therefore, unit digit =unit digit of 7<sup>3</sup> which is 3</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=116 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image007.png\"></p><p>We know, that cyclicity of 7 is 4</p><p>So, when we divide 143 by 4 we get 3 as reminder,</p><p>Therefore, unit digit =unit digit of 7<sup>3</sup> which is 3</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;Three partners A, B and C started a business by investing a total amount of Rs.45000. A invested 25(&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">5", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2344;&#2375; 45000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; A &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; 25(5/9)% &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, B &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2351;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 23 : 28 : 25 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.12500", "Rs.17500", "Rs.22500", "Rs.20500"], "options_hi": ["12500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "17500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "22500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "20500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>A's investment = 25(5/9)% of 45000 = 11500</p><p>Let C's investment = a</p><p>Then, B's investment = 45000  -  11500  -  a = 33500  -  a</p><p>Then, profit ratio, A: B: C = (12 * 11500): (8 * (33500  -  a)): (12 * a) = 23: 28: 25</p><p><b>a = Rs.12500</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A's investment = 25(5/9)% of 45000 = 11500</p><p>Let C's investment = a</p><p>Then, B's investment = 45000  -  11500  -  a = 33500  -  a</p><p>Then, profit ratio, A: B: C = (12 * 11500): (8 * (33500  -  a)): (12 * a) = 23: 28: 25</p><p><b>a = Rs.12500</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cone-shaped storage tank's height and radius are 9 and 7 feet, respectively. Determine how much liquid the tank can contain. (Take &#960; = 3.14)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2306;&#2337;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 9 &#2324;&#2352; 7 &#2347;&#2368;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2340;&#2352;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; (&#960; = 3.14 &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;)</p>", "options_en": ["471 cubic feet", "450 cubic feet", "435.32 cubic feet", "461.58 cubic feet"], "options_hi": ["471 &#2328;&#2344; &#2347;&#2368;&#2335;", "450 &#2328;&#2344; &#2347;&#2368;&#2335;", "435.32 &#2328;&#2344; &#2347;&#2368;&#2335;", "461.58 &#2328;&#2344; &#2347;&#2368;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Quantity of liquid in the tank = Volume of the tank = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h/3</p><p>= (1/3) * 3.14 * 7<sup>2</sup> * 9</p><p>= 461.58 cubic feet</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Quantity of liquid in the tank = Volume of the tank = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h/3</p><p>= (1/3) * 3.14 * 7<sup>2</sup> * 9</p><p>= 461.58 cubic feet</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sum of Rs. 2000 is invested at 10% rate of simple interest. What is the total amount obtained after 8 years?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; 10% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 8 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 3000", "Rs. 3600", "Rs. 4000", "Rs. 4200"], "options_hi": ["3000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319;", "3600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319;", "4000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319;", "4200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Interest obtained after 8 years = (2000 * 10 * 8)/100 = Rs. 1600</p><p>Total amount = 2000 + 1600 = Rs. 3600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Interest obtained after 8 years = (2000 * 10 * 8)/100 = Rs. 1600</p><p>Total amount = 2000 + 1600 = Rs. 3600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Given that sin&#952; =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">15", "q_hi": "&#2351;&#2361; &#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; sin&#952; = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">15", "options_en": ["23/49", "49/23", "26/3", "26/23"], "options_hi": ["23/49", "49/23", "26/3", "26/23"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>By using sin&#952;=15/17, cos&#952;=8/17, tan&#952;=15/8, cot&#952;=8/15, and sec&#952;=17/8, substitute directly into the expression to get the numerator = 15 X (8/15) + 17 X (15/17) = 23 and the denominator = 8 X (15/8) + 16 X (17/8) = 49, so the value is 23/49.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>By using sin&#952;=15/17, cos&#952;=8/17, tan&#952;=15/8, cot&#952;=8/15, and sec&#952;=17/8, substitute directly into the expression to get the numerator = 15 X (8/15) + 17 X (15/17) = 23 and the denominator = 8 X (15/8) + 16 X (17/8) = 49, so the value is 23/49.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the adjoining figure A, B, C and D are concyclic points. Find the value of x.</p><p><img width=298 height=251 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/17991/image002.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; A, B, C &#2324;&#2352; D &#2360;&#2350;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"298\" height=\"251\" id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/17991/image002.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["85&#730;", "105&#730;", "95&#730;", "115&#730;"], "options_hi": ["85&#730;", "105&#730;", "95&#730;", "115&#730;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>&#8736;ABC = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p> <p>&#8736;ADC = 180&#730;- 95&#730; = 85&#730;(opposite angles of cyclic quadrilateral)</p> <p>X = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8736;ABC = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p> <p>&#8736;ADC = 180&#730;- 95&#730; = 85&#730;(opposite angles of cyclic quadrilateral)</p> <p>X = 180&#730;- 85&#730; = 95&#730;(linear pair)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>&#160;Average of all natural&nbsp;numbers between 1268 and 1986 is __________.</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>1268 &#2324;&#2352; 1986 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; _____ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1645", "1598", "1627", "1823"], "options_hi": ["1645", "1598", "1627", "1823"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>\"Average of an arithmetic progression = (First term + last term)/2</p><p>So the first no&nbsp;is 1269 and the last number is 1985</p><p>Average=(first+last)/2</p><p>Average = (1269 + 1985)/2 = 1627</p><p>\"</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>\"Average of an arithmetic progression = (First term + last term)/2</p><p>So the first no&nbsp;is 1269 and the last number is 1985</p><p>Average=(first+last)/2</p><p>Average = (1269 + 1985)/2 = 1627</p><p>\"</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}]}